SUMMARY:History at Home: 100 Years of the Garden Club of Montclair
DESCRIPTION:Founded in 1926\, the Garden Club of Montclair is celebrating 100 years of service to the Montclair community through education\, artistry\, and connection centered around conservation\, flower design and horticulture. At this History at Home we’ll be joined by Garden Club member Cynthia Corhan-Aitken for a screening of the anniversary documentary 100: A Century in Bloom created by Alex Pavljuk\, Creative Media Producer at Montclair Art Museum. Hear the legacy and stories of Garden Club members as they approach the A Century in Bloom Standard Flower Show at the Van Vleck House & Gardens from September 25th to 27th. \nThis is a free program held on zoom\, register for the zoom link here: https://events.humanitix.com/history-at-home-100-years-of-the-garden-club-of-montclair/tickets \nShare this:\n				Share on Facebook (Opens in new window)\n				Facebook\n			\n				Share on Bluesky (Opens in new window)\n				Bluesky\n			\n				Share on LinkedIn (Opens in new window)\n				LinkedIn\n			\n				Share on Threads (Opens in new window)\n				Threads\n			\n				Share on Nextdoor (Opens in new window)\n				Nextdoor\n			\n				Share on WhatsApp (Opens in new window)\n				WhatsApp\n			\n				Email a link to a friend (Opens in new window)\n				Email
